# Notebooks are generated artifacts: scripts/sync_notebooks_to_jlite.py
# rewrites jupyterlite/content/ on every CI docs build, and that build runs on
# Linux. Without this, a notebook written on Windows (the pixi env here is a
# Windows build) lands as CRLF, and the next Linux sync rewrites every line --
# turning a one-cell change into a whole-file diff.
#
# After adding or changing a rule here, run once:
#     git add --renormalize . && git commit -m "normalize notebook line endings"
*.ipynb text eol=lf

# Same reasoning, different generator. specl-translate and `specl-validate
# score --history` write LF unconditionally, and the docs CI job regenerates
# both on Linux. Pinning them stops a Windows-side regeneration from rewriting
# every line and burying the actual spec change.
docs/SPEC.ttl         text eol=lf
docs/spec-history.ttl text eol=lf
